**Summary:**

The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The `first_word()` function was returning `parts[1]` instead of `parts[0]`. 

This caused:
- `first_word('hello world')` to return 'world' instead of 'hello'
- `first_word('solo')` to raise an IndexError

The fix was simple: changed `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]` to correctly return the first element of the split array. All tests now pass.
